{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Spoon-shaped curette.jpg|right|thumb|A spoon-shaped '''curette''' in sterile packaging]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|curette}}, from {{m|fr|curer||to clean out, scrape out}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kjʊˈɹɛt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-curette.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|noun}} {{lb|en|medicine|dentistry}} A hand-held [[surgical]] [[instrument]], often with a [[scoop]] or [[hook]] at its tip, used for [[cleaning]] or [[debride|debriding]] [[biological]] [[tissue]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Cecilia Gorrel|title=Small Animal Dentistry|publisher=Elsevier (Saunders)|url=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=lsxmjZKyNhgC&pg=PA223&dq=%22curette%22%7C%22curettes%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiw8YC8oqP9AhXEgVwKHZMVBCwQ6AF6BAhiEAI#v=onepage&q=%22curette%22%7C%22curettes%22&f=false|page=223
|passage='''''Curettes''''' are used for the subgingival removal of dental deposits and for root planing. They can also be used supragingivally. The working tip of a '''curette''' is more slender than that of a scaler.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Shannon Withycombe|title=Lost: Miscarriage in Nineteenth-Century America|publisher=w:Rutgers University Press|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=nz6-DwAAQBAJ&pg=PT107&dq=%22curette%22%7C%22curettes%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiw8YC8oqP9AhXEgVwKHZMVBCwQ6AF6BAhIEAI#v=onepage&q=%22curette%22%7C%22curettes%22&f=false|page=unnumbered
|passage=Beginning in the 1880s, the '''curette''' quickly became the popular choice for those doctors on the lookout for instrumental aid in cases of pregnancy loss.}}
#* '''2020''', Yu Matsumoto, ''10: Bone '''Curette''' Handle for Improved Bone Removal in Endoscopic Ear Surgery'', Seiji Kakehata, Tsukasa Ito, Daisuke Yamauchi (editors), ''Innovations in Endoscopic Ear Surgery'', Springer, [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=dbOmDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA86&dq=%22curette%22%7C%22curettes%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiw8YC8oqP9AhXEgVwKHZMVBCwQ6AF6BAhJEAI#v=onepage&q=%22curette%22%7C%22curettes%22&f=false page 86],
#*: '''Curettes''' with an octagonal-shaped shaft are readily available and widely distributed in Japan.

